  "question": {
    "text": "For $t \\gt -1$, let $\\alpha_t$ and $\\beta_t$ be the roots of the equation\n$\\left((t+2)^{\\frac{1}{7}}-1\\right) x^2+\\left((t+2)^{\\frac{1}{6}}-1\\right)$ $x+\\left((t+2)^{\\frac{1}{21}}-1\\right)=0$<br>If $\\lim _{t \\rightarrow-1^{+}} \\alpha_t=a$ and $\\lim _{t \\rightarrow-1^{+}} \\beta_t=b$, then $72(a+b)^2$ is equal to ________."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "98",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & a+b=\\lim _{t \\rightarrow-1^{+}}(\\alpha+\\beta)=\\lim _{t \\rightarrow-1^{+}}-\\frac{(t+2)^{\\frac{1}{6}}-1}{(t+2)^{\\frac{1}{7}}-1} \\\\ & \\text { let } t+2=y \\\\ & a+b=\\lim _{y \\rightarrow 1^{+}} \\frac{y^{1 / 6}-1}{y^{1 / 7}-1}=\\frac{7}{6} \\\\ & 72(a+b)^2=72 \\frac{49}{36}=98\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}